# Flask Portal Conventions

- Extend the existing shell/theme (`admin_web_theme.py`, `style.css` CSS variables, light/dark) — do not introduce a parallel design system or SPA stack.
- Public UI strings in German; admin UI stays German where it already is.
- Do not weaken auth/session/`flask-login`/Limiter; secrets only via config or env.
- Extend existing JS modules under `static/portal/`; no unnecessary new bundlers or frameworks.
- Do not invent Impressum/Datenschutz/FAQ content — maintain the existing legal/help modules.
